+			<p>“Now I’ll tell you what we’ll do,” said Hannah, when she had examined and questioned Beth; “we will have <abbr epub:type="z3998:name-title">Dr.</abbr> <span epub:type="z3998:personal-name">Bangs</span>, just to take a look at you, dear, and see that we start right; then we’ll send Amy off to Aunt March’s, for a spell, to keep her out of harm’s way, and one of you girls can stay at home and amuse Beth for a day or two.”</p>
 			<p>“I shall stay, of course; I’m oldest,” began Meg, looking anxious and self-reproachful.</p>
 			<p>“<em>I</em> shall, because it’s my fault she is sick; I told mother I’d do the errands, and I haven’t,” said Jo decidedly.</p>
 			<p>“Which will you have, Beth? there ain’t no need of but one,” said Hannah.</p>
